### PROJECT CONTEXT & STATE SUMMARY

1. Application Overview:
- Project: Production-grade, full-stack e-commerce application.
- Architecture: Layered N-Tier Architecture (Model -> Repository -> Service -> Controller).
- Backend: Spring Boot running on Port 8081.
- Frontend: Vue.js (Vue 3 with Vite/Axios, usually running on http://localhost:5173).
- Database: H2 In-Memory Database (jdbc:h2:mem:ecomdb).

2. Completed Modules & Implementation Rules:
- Entity: Product
  - Linked to Category via @ManyToOne (category field).
  - Fields: id (Long), name (String), sku (String), description (String), price (double/Double), discountPrice (Double), stockQuantity (int), imageUrl (String), brand (String), releaseYear (int/Integer), active (boolean).
  - Soft-delete pattern implemented using the `active` boolean flag.

- Repository: ProductRepository
  - Extends JpaRepository<Product, Long>.
  - Query methods:
    - findByActiveTrue()
    - findBySku(String sku)
    - findByCategoryIdAndActiveTrue(Long categoryId)
    - findByNameContainingIgnoreCaseAndActiveTrue(String name)

- Service: ProductService
  - Configured with @Service and @SuppressWarnings("null").
  - Primary logic methods:
    - getAllActiveProducts() -> uses findByActiveTrue()
    - getProductById(Long id)
    - getProductBySku(String sku)
    - getProductsByCategoryId(Long categoryId)
    - searchProductsByName(String name)
    - saveProduct(Product product)
    - updateProduct(Long id, Product productDetails) -> fetches via findById(id) first, merges non-null updated fields (including category check), and saves.
    - deactivateProduct(Long id) -> soft-deletes by setting active = false.
    - deleteProduct(Long id) -> hard deletes via existsById/deleteById.

- Controller: ProductController
  - Base path: /api/products
  - Configured with @RestController and @CrossOrigin(origins = "*").
  - Endpoints:
    - GET /api/products
    - GET /api/products/{id}
    - GET /api/products/sku/{sku}
    - GET /api/products/category/{categoryId}
    - GET /api/products/search?name=...
    - POST /api/products
    - PUT /api/products/{id}
    - PATCH /api/products/{id}/deactivate
    - DELETE /api/products/{id}

- Initializer: DataInitializer
  - Implements CommandLineRunner (@Component).
  - Pre-loads sample Categories ("Electronics", "Clothing") and linked sample Products into H2 DB automatically on startup.

3. Key Engineering Rules to Preserve:
- DO NOT use streams on repository calls when custom JPA method signatures exist (use repository-level filtering like `findByActiveTrue()`).
- Always implement explicit field updates in `updateProduct` inside Service rather than calling `saveProduct` directly from Controller.
- Keep `@CrossOrigin(origins = "*")` on Controllers for Vue.js compatibility.
- Ensure all new modules follow this exact standard: Model -> Repository -> Service -> Controller.